NAME
       ps - report a snapshot of the current processes

SYNOPSIS
       ps [-H] [--sort=pid|cpu|mem]

DESCRIPTION
       List all processes: PID, parent PID, state (R running, S ready, Z
       exited, D loading), CPU usage, resident memory, CPU time and name.
       Options aux are accepted and ignored, every process is always shown.

OPTIONS
       -H
           show the process hierarchy by indenting children

       --sort=KEY
           sort by pid (default), cpu or mem

EXAMPLES
       ps
       ps --sort=mem | head
       ps | grep sh

SEE ALSO
       kill(1), free(1)
